==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|provendre}}, from {{der|en|fro|provendre}}, variant of {{m|fro|provende||allowance, provision}}, from {{der|en|LL.|praebenda||a payment, in {{der|en|ML.|-}} also an allowance of food and drink, pittance, also a prebend}}. {{doublet|en|prebend}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈpɹɒvɪndə/|/ˈpɹɒvəndə/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈpɹɑvəndɚ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{lb|en|dated}} [[food|Food]], especially for [[livestock]].
#: {{syn|en|fodder|Thesaurus:food}}
#* {{RQ:Meredith Richard Feverel||12||The farm which supplied to him ungrudging '''provender''' had all his vast capacity for work in willing exercise …}}
#* {{RQ:Butler Hudibras|part=1|canto=[[s:Hudibras/Part 1/Canto 2|canto 2]]|passage=He ripp'd the womb up of his mother, / Dame [[Tellus]], 'cause he wanted [[fother]], / And '''provender''', wherewith to feed / Himself and his less cruel [[steed]].}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1952
|author={{w|Norman Lewis (author)|Norman Lewis}}
|title=Golden Earth
|section=
